WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.248 --> 00:00:09.696
Here are the 5 key factors to consider for a successful wedding-parent makeup booking.

2
00:00:10.032 --> 00:00:17.088
1) Check for expertise: is it a wedding-parent specialist? The first thing to check is whether the shop specializes in wedding parents, not just brides.

3
00:00:17.424 --> 00:00:26.280
Large wedding shops often run an assembly-line system, putting veteran staff on the bride and leaving the parents to weekend part-timers.

4
00:00:26.616 --> 00:00:33.048
Wedding-parent makeup has to address middle-age concerns like drooping eyelids, nasolabial folds, and thinning hair at the crown, so

5
00:00:33.384 --> 00:00:39.360
be sure to check whether a specialist with real hands-on experience and an understanding of bone structure will personally handle it.

6
00:00:39.696 --> 00:00:45.744
2) Logistics: in-shop vs. on-site makeup. How you get there affects your condition on the day.

7
00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:52.704
Visiting the shop means full facilities and equipment, but it comes with the hassle of travel and the risk of traffic.

8
00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:59.232
On-site makeup, on the other hand, lets you get ready comfortably at home or a hotel, saving time and energy.

9
00:00:59.568 --> 00:01:08.256
But if you go with on-site service, make sure it's a licensed, legitimate business to avoid no-shows or subpar work.

10
00:01:08.592 --> 00:01:15.936
3) Price: what's reasonable. In Seoul, a fair price range for wedding-parent makeup is around 200,000 to 300,000 won.

11
00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:20.736
Shops priced under 100,000 won often put a junior trainee on you, or

12
00:01:21.072 --> 00:01:27.168
tack on extra charges for wigs, false lashes, or hair fiber powder, so the final price can climb — watch out for that.

13
00:01:27.504 --> 00:01:34.368
Prioritizing skilled technique and dedicated one-on-one service over price is the secret to a choice you won't regret.

14
00:01:34.704 --> 00:01:41.520
4) Separate spaces: a private, comfortable setting. Parents are very nervous and sensitive on the wedding day.

15
00:01:41.856 --> 00:01:50.976
To avoid the awkwardness of running into your child's in-laws bare-faced, and to ease the parents' minds, choose a place with separate private rooms.

16
00:01:51.312 --> 00:01:59.208
A quiet, relaxed setting boosts the parents' emotional comfort, which carries through as a warm smile and confidence at the ceremony.

17
00:01:59.544 --> 00:02:07.896
5) Kindness and attentive care: one-on-one pre-consultation. Wedding-parent makeup has to be about more than skill — it should comfort the parents too.

18
00:02:08.232 --> 00:02:12.696
Be sure to check whether they offer a one-on-one consultation before booking.

19
00:02:13.032 --> 00:02:22.656
Meeting a specialist beforehand to share concerns and settle on a style turns the day's anxiety into confidence, letting the parents finally feel like the stars they are.

20
00:02:22.992 --> 00:02:26.376
A well-prepared parent is the most confident and beautiful.

21
00:02:26.712 --> 00:02:29.184
Compare these factors carefully.
